Package: bootplus
Title: Modern Visualization, Interpretation, and Bayesian Bootstrap Extensions for 'boot'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Aastha", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "aastha.chhabra.08@gmail.com")
Description: Extends the 'boot' package with three modern capabilities:
    (1) rich ggplot2-based visualizations of bootstrap distributions, bias, confidence intervals, and comparison plots; 
    (2) human-readable interpretation of bootstrap output including bias, standard error, and confidence intervals; 
    (3) a Bayesian bootstrap workflow using Dirichlet weighting (Rubin, 1981) with posterior summaries and credible interval visualizations. 
Designed as a non-invasive extension layer that works directly with 'boot' objects.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
